                <note rend="inline" type="source">868.48/414b: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the High Commissioner at Constantinople</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Bristol</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-03-24T15:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 24,
                                1923—3 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>50. Reports Department has received through Near East Relief indicate that
                    Turkish authorities have ordered deportation to interior of 4,500 refugees now
                    at Mersina, in case arrangements are not made for their immediate departure from
                    that port.</p>
                <p>See Department’s 44, March 16, 7 p.m. regarding refugees in Constantinople and
                    submit prompt telegraphic report regarding situation there and at other Turkish
                    ports.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
